        "title": "Linear Programming - Geometry and the Simplex Method",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A linear program optimizes a **linear objective** over a **polyhedron** defined by linear inequalities. The entire theory rests on one geometric fact: the optimum, if it exists, is achieved at a **vertex** of the feasible polyhedron. The simplex method is a disciplined walk from vertex to vertex along edges, each step improving the objective, until no improving edge remains."
